      "message": "[Medium] Short local parts give away too much.\n\nCurrent output:\n\n| local part | result | revealed |\n|---|---|---|\n| `a@x.io` | `a***@x.io` | the **whole** local part |\n| `ab@x.io` | `a***@x.io` | half of it |\n| `abc@x.io` | `a***@x.io` | 1 of 3 |\n| `abcdef@x.io` | `ab****ef@x.io` | **4 of 6** |\n\nThe fixed-width stars are good, because they hide the length. Still, a one-character address is fully revealed, and right at the 6-character threshold two thirds of it stay in clear.\n\nSuggestion: scale what is kept with the length:\n- ≤ 2 chars → `***` (nothing kept)\n- 3-5 → `a***`\n- 6-9 → `a****z`\n- ≥ 10 → `ab****yz`\n\nPlease add 1-, 2- and 3-character cases to `test_emails_are_partially_masked`.",
